    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0346" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.5151/1727: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Berlin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-01T13:00:00+01:00">August 1, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 1—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign exchange control order issued today provides “payments from Aski accounts
                    for the deliveries of goods to the United States <pb facs="0347" n="248"
                        xml:id="pg248"/> may not be made after August 3, 1936, except deliveries
                    based on contracts closed prior to August 3, 1936. Permits for private barter
                    transactions with the United States shall not be issued after August 3,
                    1936.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
